Subject: [PATCH] bus/fslmc: lower the MC version floor to 10.33

The NPE-010 ships MC firmware 10.33.0 in FlexSPI flash, but DPDK refuses the
fslmc bus below 10.39.0, so the DPAA2 fronthaul port cannot be used:

    DPAA2_BUS: DPAA2 MC version not compatible! 10.33.0 < 10.39.0
    DPAA2_BUS: Unable to map MC Portal

The floor is conservative for this board. Every DPAA2 object API matches what
DPDK 25.11 expects (DPBP 3.4, DPIO 4.3, DPCON 3.3, DPCI 3.4, DPDMAI 3.4,
DPRTC 2.3); only DPNI differs (board 8.3 vs 8.6), and the sole 8.6 dependency
is dpni_get_mac_speed_capability() for link-speed *reporting*, which is already
guarded at runtime with an explicit fallback.

Verified on the board with the floor lowered: the MC portal maps, MC commands
succeed, the scan enumerates all 23 objects of dprc.2, and the net PMD reports
"dpni.2: netdev created, connected to dpmac.6". The la12xx bbdev continues to
probe in the same process.

Validated to probe/initialise only, NOT under fronthaul traffic. Revert once
the board's MC firmware is updated to 10.39.0 (qoriq-mc-binary,
mc_lx2160a_10.39.0.itb, flash offset 0xa00000).
---
diff --git a/drivers/bus/fslmc/mc/fsl_dpmng.h b/drivers/bus/fslmc/mc/fsl_dpmng.h
--- a/drivers/bus/fslmc/mc/fsl_dpmng.h
+++ b/drivers/bus/fslmc/mc/fsl_dpmng.h
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ struct fsl_mc_io;
  * Management Complex firmware version information
  */
 #define MC_VER_MAJOR 10
-#define MC_VER_MINOR 39
+#define MC_VER_MINOR 33
 
 /**
  * struct mc_version
